                        "prompt":  "FALLOWMARCH STARTER WILDLIFE 02 — RYECREST. One original adult groundbird species for a serious medieval RPG, gleaning spilled grain and grasshoppers along Fallowmarch field margins. Compact forward-leaning body with a deep but balanced breast, short sturdy neck and strong runner legs; a clear land bird, not a tall wader. Short broad seed-cracking bill with shallow keratin ridges, small dark amber side-set eyes, complete natural bird face and closed beak. A low backward sweep of layered crown feathers and a short tidy fan tail create a distinct readable silhouette. Exactly two weight-bearing legs, each with three forward toes and a small rear toe; show both hocks, feet and claws clearly separated. Two wings folded close against the flanks, each wing reads as one clean feathered limb ready for later rigging, with no other limbs. Healthy moderate adult proportions, neither bulky nor spindly. Layered natural plumage in muted olive-brown, weathered rye-gold and warm umber, a pale cream throat, russet wing bars and charcoal feather tips, fine overlapping feather detail with varied matte sheen. Serious alert neutral expression. One whole bird in a three-quarter front standing pose, centered, full body visible, plain warm light-gray studio background, soft even light. No field scenery, straw, props, armor, text, panels, extra creatures, huge eyes, grin, horns, spikes, dinosaur anatomy or machinery.",
